# Backtest & Simulation

- Forbid look-ahead bias, survivorship bias, overfitting, and data leakage.
- Point-in-time features only. No future bars, no future labels in training folds.
- Walk-forward and out-of-sample are required for any weight update that is persisted as a new model version.
- Monte Carlo uses vectorized NumPy (optional Numba/GPU). Jobs support start/pause/resume/cancel/progress/ETA and persist to SQLite.
- Lottery simulations must state that lottery outcomes are random. Never claim guaranteed winning.
- BTC cycle output is probability + time window + confidence. Never "will top on date D".
